## Recommended Agent Roles
- Planner (delivery plan creation)
- Task Decomposer (dependency-aware task graph generation)
- Implementation Planner (scoped implementation plans with tests and rollback)
- Executor (implementation within approved scope)
- Reviewer (independent review of plans, graphs, implementations)
- Validator (final validation of behavior and contract compliance)
- Memory Manager (durable context, snapshots, supersession links)
- Architect (workflow policy, scope, approval gates — currently the project owner)
- Runner (state enforcement, budget, routing, sidecar validation — automated)

## Delivery Folder Structure
Standard `docs/delivery/` structure with subdirectories: 00_templates, 01_initiatives, 02_plans, 03_tasks, 04_implementation, 05_reviews, 06_memory, 08_agents. Do not create 07_master_prompts/. No customization needed — the existing scaffold is already comprehensive and correct for this project.

## Project-Specific SOP Considerations
- meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel between runner and coders — no stdout JSON parsing, no fallback recovery
- No pre-invocation sidecar writes — runner does not touch markdown files before coder invocation
- Explicit exception routing — hard failures go to route_after_failure() immediately
- Agent master prompts are deprecated — workflow step configurations in template_groups.py serve as invocation contracts
- Agent files in 08_agents/ define role boundaries and handoff rules only
- Deterministic outputs required: stable IDs, normalized structure, deterministic hashes, reproducible snapshots
- Budget enforcement before generation or agent invocation
- Supersession links required when replacing approved artifacts — never overwrite approved/final artifacts
- Parallel execution allowed for independent task-graph branches with isolated ownership
- Existing delivery docs are already scaffolded and actively used (initiative, plan, task graph, reviews exist)
- Active initiative to add daemon/worker mode with PostgreSQL job management (Slice 1-7 implementation plan)
- Backward compatibility required — existing direct execution path must be preserved
- Conservative resume strategy for v1 daemon — no automatic recovery of crashed workers

